From affeddab216cb7c3afed87f8fb6fedd8c5f6562b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:06:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Post-processings by kernels: fixes of an independent review

- The values at the nodes fall back to the computation element by
  element for the elements with more than 32 degrees of freedom (the
  local projections by kernels threw an exception, which terminated the
  noexcept exports), and for the Bernstein basis, which is not nodal.
- The mass matrices of the L2 projection are computed by the kernel of
  mfem-mgis for all the elements, in the ordering of the element matrices
  of MFEM (lexicographic for the tensor bases), instead of the full
  assembly of mfem::MassIntegrator for the tensor bases, which gave
  nodes to a mesh without nodes (slowing down the computations element
  by element which followed). The operator of the implicit gradient
  regularization is assembled element by element.
- The choice of the kernels for the L2 projections is made by all the
  processes, as for the values at the nodes: a local choice could lead
  the processes to different collective operations (blocking with a mesh
  mixing quadrangles and triangles). The Bernstein basis and the devices
  of libCEED (assembly without element restriction) are refused.
- The local projections use the absolute values of the determinants of
  the jacobians: the Cholesky factorization failed for elements of
  negative orientation.
- computeMeasure and computeIntegral compute the geometric data of the
  elements of the material only (computeElementsGeometry with a list of
  elements): the data of the whole mesh were computed for each material
  (49.8 s instead of 0.04 s for 1000 materials).
- The lexicographic ordering of the dofs is copied from the finite element
  before being read on the device (the debug device protected the memory
  of the finite element on the host).
- An invalid MFEM_MGIS_POST_PROCESSINGS_COMPUTATION is reported by
  initialize. gatherValues refuses more values than an int can index.
- PostProcessingsKernelsTest: non finite values detected, check that the
  mesh is not given nodes, variants with the dofs ordered by vector
  dimension and of order 3 (values at the nodes element by element).
- Documentation updated.
---
